From: Wren <wren@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] gstreamer: WPE_SHELL_DISABLE_MEDIA_DISK_CACHE also stops urisourcebin's download buffer

The playbin "download" flag honoured it, but urisourcebin's "download" property was set for every
preload=auto player. On 32-bit systems GStreamer's downloadbuffer/sparse file keep offsets in gsize and wrap
at 4 GiB, so files over 4 GiB with the moov at the end never played (LG TV, 2026-11-19).
---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
index ee21208..46fe4c0 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
@@ -2804,7 +2804,7 @@ void MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer::configureElement(GstElement* element)
     if (startsWith(name.span(), "urisourcebin"_s) && !m_isLegacyPlaybin && m_preload == MediaPlayer::Preload::Auto) {
         if (isBlob)
             g_object_set(element, "ring-buffer-max-size", static_cast<guint64>(2 * MB), nullptr);
-        else if (!isMediaSource() && !isMediaStreamPlayer())
+        else if (!isMediaSource() && !isMediaStreamPlayer() && !isMediaDiskCacheDisabled())
             g_object_set(element, "download", TRUE, nullptr);
     }
 
